{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאבדם", :translit "va-yavidam", :gloss "and He destroyed them"} {:he "ויאבדם ה' עד היום", :translit "va-yavidam Adonai ad ha-yom", :gloss "and the Lord destroyed them until this day"} {:he "משגיא לגוים ויאבדם", :translit "mashgia la-goyim va-yavidam", :gloss "He leads nations astray and destroys them"} {:he "ב'", :translit "bet", :gloss "two [occurrences]"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויאבדם ה' עד היום" "משגיא לגוים ויאבדם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic link between the two occurrences of ויאבדם via the shared word and the story of Pharaoh lured into the sea."}], :frame {:text "At the splitting of the sea, God caused Pharaoh to see a vision of a female mare at the edge of the water, so that the Egyptian horses would charge in to mate, dragging the army into the sea to its destruction. This explains the verse in Psalm 9:6, משגיא לגוים ויאבדם, 'You rebuke the nations, You destroy the wicked,' as referring to Pharaoh. The Ba'al HaTurim connects this to the two biblical occurrences of the word ויאבדם — one here in Deuteronomy 11:4 describing the drowning of the Egyptians, and one in Psalm 9:6.", :sources ["Tanchuma, Beshallah 11" "Psalm 9:6" "Deuteronomy 11:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויאבדם ה' עד היום" "משגיא לגוים ויאבדם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויאבדם ה' עד היום", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "משגיא לגוים ויאבדם", :refs ["Job 12:23"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic link between the two occurrences of ויאבדם via the shared word and the story of Pharaoh lured into the sea.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:50.103900192Z", :model "glm-5.2"}